course: dictionary
lesson: 1962
title: Compassion
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Compassion is a strong feeling of sympathy for someone who is suffering, and a wish to help them. It means caring about other people's pain. Look at the words around it: «Humanists believe this life is the only one and that people can be good using reason and compassion (caring about other people's pain), without God.» The brackets give you the meaning.
explain: Compassion is a noun, and you can say «show compassion», «feel compassion for», «with compassion» or «full of compassion». Each phrase describes how someone cares for another person. Try swapping in the meaning: "using reason and caring about other people's pain" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: In a story, a character's compassion may make them help others even when it is hard. Caring about pain is not always easy, and it often needs courage. Ask yourself: what does this person do, and why? The answer often shows what compassion means.
fact: Compassion is a noun, so you can say «show compassion», «feel compassion for» or «full of compassion».
fact: «Compassion» means a strong feeling of sympathy for someone who is suffering, and a wish to help them.
fact: In the Good Samaritan story, a man shows compassion to a hurt man, even though helping is hard.
fact: Humanists, who think this life is the only one, try to be good using reason and compassion.
fact: Compassion is a key value in ethics and religion lessons.
exercise: «The children showed compassion to the lost puppy and carried it home.» What does compassion mean here? | Playing a game with it | Being angry with the puppy | *Caring about its pain and wanting to help | Ignoring it because it is noisy
exercise: «The nurse looked at the hurt man with compassion.» What does with compassion suggest? | With a loud shout | Without looking at him | *With caring and sympathy | With a bored yawn
exercise: Humanists live good lives by reason and compassion. Which word is closest in meaning to compassion? | Anger | Boredom | *Sympathy | Speed
test: «Humanists believe people can be good using reason and compassion.» In this sentence, compassion means what? | *Caring about other people's pain | Being very rich | Knowing many facts | Winning every game
test: In stories, a character's compassion makes them help others even when it is hard. What does this show? | *Compassion can lead a person to act kindly even when it costs them | Compassion means being scared of others | Compassion is only for animals | Compassion means never helping anyone
exam: Jayden says, «I feel compassion for the boy who fell.» What does Jayden feel? | Joy that the boy fell | Anger that the boy fell | Boredom | *Sorrow for the boy's pain and a wish to help him
